  "loc": "Abstract, p.1; Section 2 Model, p.8-9",
  "quote": "We model the conference-author interactions as a Stackelberg game",
  "note": "The main object is a conference peer-review and resubmission game between a conference and authors. Reviews are i.i.d. noisy signals of paper quality, and reviewers have no agency ('they have no agency in our game-theoretic formulation'). The acceptance policy is a statistical decision rule on signals, not a voting procedure that aggregates agents' inputs into a collective decision. Coding stopped."
